# The simplifier over a whole program as ir/simplify.ts calls it (item term-self-host-001-0086, spec 4.9): whether a
# `let` is a host global is read here, where the face handed ir/simplifying.tree a TypeScript closure
# (`statement.foreign !== undefined`). The mill writes `foreign` only as a host's written or own name, never empty
# (compile/minting-flow.tree, `text-else`), and node-json leaves an empty one out (decision 034 section 2), so a `let`
# whose `foreign` is not empty is exactly one whose `foreign` was set.

load ../compile/node
  find statement

load ./simplifying
  find simplify

# whether a statement is a `let` of a host global
task let-is-host-global
  take given, like statement
  like boolean
  mark private

  sift given
    case let
      link foreign
      back is-unequal(foreign, <>)
    miss
      back false

# run the simplifier over a whole program, `roots` the entry module's public functions when given
task simplify-program
  take program, like list, like statement
  take roots, like maybe, like list, like text
  like list, like statement

  back simplify(program, roots, let-is-host-global)
